WEBVTT

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.240
Who are the Abh?

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.490
They are parts to a machine.

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:24.200
To them, children are nothing more than replacement parts.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:31.500
Their children are mere objects to which they are able to pass on their abilities before they perish.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.260
Then what is this machine?

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:41.930
The machine is the monstrous, evil Humankind Empire Abh.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:48.850
Healthy human societies were constantly under threat from this evil machine.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:55.900
Should humanity continue to allow this machine to exist human society would surely be swallowed up.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:00.620
This machine must be destroyed.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:06.870
From speech delivered to the Central Council of the United Mankind by Councilor Fitzdavid.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:41.320
Slachoth Gothlautr

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.320
Battle of Gosroth

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.460
Lairia, report!

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.900
Direction, 78 degrees off our bow...

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:02.560
...distance, 1539.17 cédlairhs.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.200
Their course is 18 degrees.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:05.890
Sfagnomr is in that direction.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:09.030
We've sighted 120 space-time bubbles...

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.700
...of approximately 90 zaisacbau each.

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:15.470
That would amount to the total output of 4 battle divisions.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.710
Do you know which saudec they entered from?

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.680
I've narrowed it down to 47...

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:21.980
...but I can't narrow it down any further.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.050
Are any of them presently in use?

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:26.480
No.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.890
These saudecs are all closed, and all generally neglected.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:34.550
Are there any saudecs within a light year of inhabited planets?

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:37.530
Not one.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.130
Any within five light years?

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:43.630
There's one!

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:44.940
Where?

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.280
Four point one light years from Saudec Keish 193...

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.280
...is Vascotton 4 of the Vascotton system.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.800
That planet's occupied by...

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.640
...the United Mankind.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.910
A change in the enemy's space-time bubbles!

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.220
One space-time bubble has just split into ten.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.420
They've shifted their course toward us.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.460
From its size...

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.660
...the space-time bubbles appear to correspond to each ship.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.370
Executive officer,

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:13.960
put us into combat status 2.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.310
At 20:30...

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.870
...we'll to go combat status 1.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.670
Aye-aye.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.970
Captain! I couldn't!

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.980
Allow me to speak plainly.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.750
I am an Abriel.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.780
I'd lose face as an Abriel if I ran away from the enemy.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.720
Quit your petty outbursts and your boasting...

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.160
...at least until you've earned your wings...

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.630
...Ablïarsec néïc Dubreuscr Bœrh Parhynr...

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.620
...Lafiel!

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:41.630
What do you mean by running away from the enemy?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.130
You're not attached to any of the battle divisions.

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:45.800
You are still not ready.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.740
Nothing more than an extra body.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.440
But I assigned you a mission.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.940
An important mission to evacuate His Excellency, a non-combatant...

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:56.580
...from the battle area and inform the Empire...

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.480
...that we are being approached by what is likely an enemy fleet.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:03.610
Evading my order is an example of running away from the enemy.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.320
So ignorant that you don't know what running away is.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.160
If that's not losing face...

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.930
...then the Abriels are not worthy of Abh loyalty.

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.100
If you still want to argue, I'll cite you for insubordination.

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:18.760
And you can deal with it at the imperial tribunal.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.670
It was a misunderstanding on my part...

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.210
...Captain.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.510
Now, go on.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.520
I'll see you in Lacmhacarh, my precious Royal Highness.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.560
Yes. Certainly.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:58.970
Captain.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.680
We're within hailing range...

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.510
...of the unidentified space-time bubbles.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.710
Declare ourselves to them...

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.580
...and get them to identify themselves.

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:08.520
Aye-aye.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:13.520
Why, this is...!

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:20.790
This is no correspondence!

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.930
This is a challenge to battle!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:26.830
That confirms it.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.270
The signal will not stop.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:31.840
Should we respond to it?

00:06:32.670 --> 00:06:34.730
Don't bother, just ignore it.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:38.710
If they want to play, let them try to catch up to us.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:45.510
Lafiel...

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.010
Hey, Lafiel...

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.390
You bear the title of Bœrh Parhynr, right?

00:06:54.410 --> 00:06:55.960
Yes, I do.

00:06:56.570 --> 00:06:59.170
Could you tell me about your domain?

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.070
What kind of place is the domain of Parhynr?

00:07:02.070 --> 00:07:05.730
They call it rose country, so I guess there are a lot of roses.

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:07.240
Not at all.

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.610
You won't even find weeds, let alone roses.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.710
Not even microorganisms living on those planets.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.610
Then, why do they call it rose country?

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:19.290
The man who surveyed the region loved flowers...

00:07:19.450 --> 00:07:22.150
...so he'd give flower names to the territories.

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.190
There's also lily country, and camellia country.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.530
That's all it is.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:27.800
Really?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.460
So, what kind place is it?

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.130
There's nothing special about it.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:34.440
There's a yellow star...

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.500
...with seven planets orbiting it.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:40.330
The second planet may be habitable with some work.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:44.010
Maybe someday I'll make a project of it...

00:07:44.010 --> 00:07:45.810
...after I'm relieved of my royal duties.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.910
I'd love to cover the land with roses, and so justify its name.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.120
That's a beautiful thought.

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:53.110
Isn't it?

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.350
Jinto?

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.420
What is it?

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:04.260
I want to thank you.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:05.770
For what?

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.170
You're trying to comfort me.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.840
I really can't say I'm feeling any better...

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:14.330
...but I'm very grateful for your concern.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.180
Sorry if I'm not of much use.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.180
What's your home planet like?

00:08:22.750 --> 00:08:25.380
Unlike you, I have a lot to talk about.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.590
I'd love to take you to my home planet...

00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:33.400
...and have you live there a few years.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:34.790
Really?

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:38.630
That might not be a bad idea, after I'm relieved of my duties.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:40.700
I'd like that.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:45.540
<i>You've forgotten one thing.</i>

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:50.150
<i>You will have grown very little...</i>

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:52.410
<i>...and still look just as young and beautiful.</i>

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:57.210
<i>But I will have either grown old or passed away.</i>

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.160
20:30

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.710
It's time, Captain.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:04.390
All right.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.220
<i>This is the captain speaking.</i>

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.070
<i>The unidentified space-time bubbles...</i>

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.330
<i>...have clearly taken a hostile stance.</i>

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.090
<i>As of now, we're going to combat status 1.</i>

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.640
<i>All personnel, report to your combat stations.</i>

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.530
All personnel standing by at combat stations.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:49.600
Prepare to deploy mines.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.670
Charge mines 7 to 10...

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.730
...with anti-matter fuel.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:56.450
Charging mines 7 to 10...

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.790
...with anti-matter fuel.

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.590
Charging anti-matter fuel complete.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.770
Release mines.

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.630
Position them within our space-time bubble.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.640
Release mines.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:32.910
The mines are positioned within our space-time bubble.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:39.350
It's a shame we wasted mines 1 through 6 in a mock battle.

00:10:39.420 --> 00:10:42.320
But what's done is done.

00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:48.770
21:13

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.800
Enemy space-time bubbles entering the mine range.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:55.760
A textbook attack formation.

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:59.300
Generate space-time bubbles from the mines.

00:10:59.780 --> 00:11:02.540
Generating space-time bubbles from mines.

00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:11.550
Space-time bubble generation confirmed.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:17.060
Aim mines 7 at 3, 8 at 1, 9 at 6, and 10 at 7.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:18.760
Input settings...

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:22.030
7 at 3, 8 at 1, 9 at 6, and 10 at 7.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:24.060
Settings complete.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:26.730
Prepare for space combat.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:28.530
Ignite main engines.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:29.840
Aye-aye.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.170
Igniting main engines.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.140
Weapons Officer...

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:42.240
Prepare electromagnetic cannons.

00:11:42.420 --> 00:11:43.580
Aye-aye.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:47.050
Preparing electromagnetic cannons.

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:04.130
Electromagnetic cannon preparations complete.

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:07.240
Deesh...

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.270
Do you think we can win?

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:14.680
I feel the same way you do.

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:15.740
Really?

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.350
I'm betting on my genes.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.090
Me too...

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.700
21:32

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:27.790
Captain.

00:12:27.860 --> 00:12:31.160
The enemy space-time bubbles have completely surrounded us.

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:34.140
The enemy has really practiced.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.100
Their advance is a textbook case.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:41.270
However, we're just as well trained.

00:12:42.410 --> 00:12:44.280
Me and my precious crew.

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.980
Okay, here we go.

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:54.120
It's the moment you've waited for.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.180
Commence battle!

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.130
Separate all mines.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.560
Separating all mines.

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:14.730
Mine 7 to space-time separation.

00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:16.740
Mine 8 to space-time separation.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:18.150
Mine 9 to space-time separation.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.050
Mine 10 to space-time separation.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.910
Mine 8 converging with enemy bubble.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.580
Enemy ship 1...

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:28.850
...destroyed!

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.460
Mine 10 converging with enemy bubble.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:31.830
Enemy ship 7...

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:32.820
...destroyed.

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:35.060
Mine 7 converging with enemy bubble.

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.550
Enemy ship 3, destroyed.

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.300
Mine 9 converging with enemy ship.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.630
Enemy 6...

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.160
Unaffected!

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:44.910
Come about!

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.010
Forty degrees right!

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:47.700
Head straight for enemy ship 4!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:48.940
Aye-aye!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.250
Distance, 100 ches cédlairh...

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.050
...80 ches cédlairh...

00:13:56.050 --> 00:13:57.450
...60 ches cédlairh.

00:13:58.750 --> 00:14:00.090
About to converge with enemy bubble!

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:00.850
Position...

00:14:02.190 --> 00:14:04.160
Aim bow to convergence point!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.300
Fire immediately upon convergence.

00:14:09.860 --> 00:14:10.520
Aye-aye!

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.830
All units, prepare to fire electromagnetic cannons.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:19.400
Space-time convergence!

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.230
Fire!

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.520
Six more ships!

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.460
Enemy ship 4, destroyed!

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:49.870
Space-time convergence.

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:53.740
Enemy ships 2, 5, 6, 10...

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.010
Bow!

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.210
To enemy 2 convergence point!

00:14:58.510 --> 00:14:59.480
Fire!

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:06.820
Stern!

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:14.590
Enemy ships 6 and 2, destroyed!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.030
Four more vessels.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.130
Enemy ship 5, approaching broadside!

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:27.800
Not enough time for either bow or stern!

00:15:28.210 --> 00:15:30.540
Counter with mobile cannons.

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:38.520
Fire!

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.260
Come about 30 degrees left!

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:51.490
It's coming!

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.960
Focus the magnetic defense field to one side.

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:56.800
Be prepared for impact!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:13.750
Number 2 rear nozzle, damaged!

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.020
Section 310, depressurizing!

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:18.780
Emergency partitions 3 to 7 have closed.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.520
Maneuverability reduced by 15%.

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:22.560
Entering fire range...

00:16:22.560 --> 00:16:24.400
...for electromagnetic cannons.

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.700
Come about 15 degrees to right after firing.

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:29.100
Aye-aye!

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:41.050
Enemy ships 8 and 9...

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.450
...converging!

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.580
Enemy ship 10 at port-stern!

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:51.720
Stern cannons! All units fire!

00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:06.000
I'm ashamed...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:07.370
...of myself.

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:12.450
I was useless...

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.710
...at such an important time.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:18.050
How can you say that?

00:17:19.490 --> 00:17:21.850
You've been plenty helpful to me.

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:26.730
I've got only you to rely on now.

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:31.500
Or, is my life not important enough...

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:33.630
...to satisfy your proud sense of duty?

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:37.210
I was mistaken.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:38.500
You must forgive me.

00:17:39.510 --> 00:17:43.030
If you're worried about Gosroth, I'm sure they're okay.

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:45.140
You're right.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:48.410
I'm sure they are.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.850
<i>I was trying to convince myself.</i>

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.290
I'm so fond of everyone on the Gosroth.

00:17:56.620 --> 00:18:00.360
I especially respect Captain Laicch.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:02.830
I hope they're all right.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:03.830
Everyone.

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:09.900
Hey, Jinto.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:14.840
Do you remember the story about my birth secret?

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:17.340
What is it, all of a sudden?

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:18.910
Don't tell anyone.

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:20.680
This is just between us.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:21.780
Great.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:23.910
I love secrets.

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.860
Well, my...

00:18:27.860 --> 00:18:29.950
The supplier of my genes is...

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:36.400
23:05

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.910
Section closed!

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.500
Two more ships!

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:49.780
Number 7 anti-proton cannon destroyed!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:51.510
Closing all partitions!

00:18:51.550 --> 00:18:53.110
Portside armaments destroyed!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:54.480
Heavy damage to beam cannons 3 and 4!

00:18:55.320 --> 00:18:57.980
Number 3 front nozzle, inoperable!

00:18:58.550 --> 00:19:01.550
<i>Main engine output down by 61.9%!</i>

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:05.990
Abandoning Section 7.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:09.330
Divide into groups of five and join the emergency repairs!

00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.270
Sections closed, 42.

00:19:17.270 --> 00:19:20.800
Total killed, wounded and missing, 55!

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:33.390
Captain!

00:19:33.390 --> 00:19:35.760
Magnetic defense field will not hold!

00:19:35.760 --> 00:19:37.890
Firing units, don't let up.

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:41.020
We'll lure enemy 8 into range of our electromagnetic cannons!

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:42.930
Please.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:45.590
Hang in there a bit longer. A bit longer.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:58.770
Keep going, for just a bit more.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.480
Number 4 rear nozzle has been destroyed!

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:06.480
Stern!

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.450
Fire!

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:20.560
One more ship!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.280
Captain.

00:20:36.150 --> 00:20:37.990
The magnetic defense field...

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:40.420
...has been eliminated.

00:20:46.630 --> 00:20:48.400
Don't ever give up...

00:20:48.400 --> 00:20:50.360
...my dear precious crew!

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:55.030
We're going to eliminate it from our space.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:58.530
Ship's bow!

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:05.840
Aim all mobile cannons to the right side of enemy ship!

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:08.380
We'll ram them with our bow!

00:21:36.480 --> 00:21:39.340
The one who supplied my genes...

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:43.180
...was Captain Laicch.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:48.320
I was a daughter of love.

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:52.380
My father loved the Captain.

00:21:53.230 --> 00:21:56.960
I thought that might be the case.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.870
I hoped it would be.

